  people don't even read the job  application properly did you see how a  computer programmer I'm gonna apply  takes them two seconds and it turns your  time out but then you go through that  process right okay I'm gonna weed them  out traditional HR process I'm gonna  weed them out we're gonna go through  interviews again days and days and days  of your time sorting through interviews  and finally you get the right person or  any think this this is the right person  we know we've vetted them we've checked  their references  they've interviewed with with you and  anybody else in your team your advisors  whoever finally the right person and  then you actually put them on the job  and how often does it actually work out  and you go through that three-month  trial period  so many people end up being fired or  quit in that process and you already  know within the first day and that's  gonna work or not but you've invested so  much into them into that whole process  of hiring that you are trying to find  and make it wait awake at work because  you don't want to go back to what it was  before you want to go and do that whole  painful process all over again so  eliminate the process and create a new  one that works for you I've made a video  about why the hiring process is broken  and how I use it you should check it out  it's a great resource but stop doing  resumes stop looking at covers letters  stop looking at interviews because those  are not the skills you're hiring for  number three hire passionate problem  solvers the number one ingredient that  you want in a new employee coming on is  someone who is passionate there's an  expression that you know I'd rather have  somebody who has ignorant on fire  instead of knowledge on ice you want the  person who is burning to be in your  business the person who will bust  through brick walls will solve any  problems right as an entrepreneur you're  running up against a million problems  every day right it's not a defined set  of problems it's gonna change as you  grow and build your empire and you need  people who will be resourceful and will  find solutions and people I've had on my  team me have had zero skills in the area  that now they're gonna get into but  they're willing to dive in I'll win  figure it out and not be told here's how  to do it  XYZ because they are passionate problem  solvers I've hired people who are there  total misfits they look terrible on  paper nobody would give these guys a  chance but they work hard they love what  they do they're committed to what my  business is all about  and they'll invest anything to go out  and find a way to make something happen  that's what you need so stop looking for  specific skills and look for people who  are passionate problem solvers because  often the guys who look the best on  paper end up being the worst employees  number four give opportunities to  explore there's nothing worse than  coming to a job and doing the same  thing over and over and over and over  and over and over again right would you  like that  that's why why you left your old job so  why are you being that kind of boss to  somebody else give people opportunities  to explore what they're good at what  they love because you are not the genius  of everything okay  you are not the expert at everything  give people a chance to explore what  they're good at  explore the creativity and bring that to  the business because they'll feel a lot  more fulfilled and you'll end up with a  much greater product than if you're just  slapping wrists and saying this is the  only exact way to do it so an example  that you guys can relate to I put out a  video not too long ago with the Beatles  success story and my initial vision was  to have you know the Beatles just their  video playing and me popping in texts  talking about their early struggles and  how they overcame them and Kristine I  was my video editor hey Christina  she she did that and then added her own  feel to it she added Beals pictures in  there and sometimes blocked out the  picture completely and and she made it  way better than what I had in my head  right I could have said no do it exactly  like this is the only way I want to do  it and wouldn't make Christina feel  restricted not happy but also we've had  a worse product right give people that  opportunity to explore the reason why I  hired Christina in the first place was  in that first job assignment that I gave  her and I gave 20 other people who are  applying to be my video editor she  didn't just do what I asked most people  just gave me what I asked right they did  the bare minimum they did they did what  I told him to do that's not good enough  she went beyond and she took the Vita  that I asked her to do it added some  Christina spice and magic to it like yes  the one person who did something  different who explored who pushed the  limits who thought of new ideas so I  don't have to do everything myself and  that's why I hired her and that's why  she's awesome and that's why she's still  working and going crazy making these  videos for us so you need to give people  that opportunity to explore and number  five make sure you have the time you  have to make sure you give yourself to  your team right there's nothing it's so  it's so bad when an employee comes to  work at the business and they're they're  thrown in they don't know what they're  doing they don't have the training they  can access you there's no way  connect with you really and there  they're feeling hopeless and a little  lost you got to make sure that when  you're bringing somebody on board you  free up your time to you will to train  them and answer their questions and  support them and when they're struggling  at the start be there guide them  motivate them remind them of what  they're doing right that that one-to-one  resource is huge and I know a lot of  entrepreneurs you know you're you're  running crazy businesses you're putting  in so many hours you know you're hiring  this person to take work away from you  now you gotta invest time into them you  may feel like you know I don't want to  do all that well if you're not willing  to invest in your team and be there for  them you have to be a great manager and  that seems not gonna love working for  you so especially at that start you got  to make yourself available you got to be  there to coach them and support them and  mentor them and teach them and train  them and don't just throw them to the  walls that will help you attract a lot  more of an all-star caliber employee  believe those you're watching like the  video you can subscribe to the channel  below and thank you so much I'll see you  soon make sure to check out my  newsletter ya got 11 hi I'm Jason G  responds Iike Rosalyn calm and I want to  say Evan Carmichael's newsletter is  consistent fun inspiring and it's the  only newsletter I prioritize and look  forward to period
 

